  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q74-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=ax^2+bx+2$. Given $f(-3)=f(5)=6$, find the values of $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p51-q74-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=\\frac{4}{15},\\qquad b=-\\frac{8}{15}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p51-q74-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Equal function values give the symmetry axis ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "b=-2a",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and substitute ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f(-3)=6",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "If $a=0$, the conditions require $-3b=4$ and $5b=4$, which cannot both hold. Hence $a\\ne0$.\n\nThe equal function values place the symmetry axis halfway between $x=-3$ and $x=5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-3+5}{2}\\\\x&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the axis formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{b}{2a}&=1\\\\b&=-2a.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $f(-3)=6$:\n$$\\begin{align*}9a-3b+2&=6\\\\9a-3(-2a)+2&=6\\\\15a&=4\\\\a&=\\frac{4}{15}\\\\b&=-2\\left(\\frac{4}{15}\\right)\\\\b&=-\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck the other given value:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(5)&=\\frac{4}{15}(5)^2-\\frac{8}{15}(5)+2\\\\f(5)&=6.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 88
  },
